  "nl_text": "The rschema_0352 database is designed to manage information about suppliers, customers, products, invoices, and the products included in those invoices. The Supplier table stores details about each supplier, including their address, ID, name, and phone number, with the Supplier_ID serving as the primary key to uniquely identify each supplier. The Customer table holds information about each customer, such as their address, ID, email, first name, last name, and phone number, with the Customer_ID being the primary key. The Product table contains details about each product, including its description, minimum stock quantity, name, purchase price, selling price, stock quantity, and the ID of the supplier from which it was sourced, with the Product_ID being the primary key and the Supplier_ID referencing the Supplier table to establish the relationship between suppliers and products. The Invoice table stores information about each invoice, including the customer's ID, date, invoice ID, tax amount, and total value, with the Invoice_ID serving as the primary key and the Customer_ID referencing the Customer table to link each invoice to its corresponding customer. The Invoice_Product table links each product to the invoices it appears on, with the Invoice_ID and Product_ID forming a composite primary key and referencing the Invoice and Product tables, respectively, to establish the relationships between products and invoices.",
  "gold_question": "Retail Management System\n\n1. Supplier Management\nRecord the basic information of suppliers, including supplier ID name, address, and phone number.\nYou can query and manage supplier information.\n\n2. Customer Management\nRecord the basic information of customers, including customer ID, first name, last name, phone number, address, email, etc.\nYou can query and manage customer information.\n\n3. Product Management\nRecord the detailed information of products, including name, description, purchase price, selling price, inventory quantity, and minimum inventory quantity.\nBy associating supplier information with supplier ID, you can track the supplier of the product.\nYou can query and manage product information, including inventory management.\n\n4. Invoice Management\nRecord the detailed information of each invoice, including invoice ID, date, tax amount, total value, and customer information.\nBy associating customer information with customer ID number, you can track the customer of the invoice.\nYou can generate and manage invoices.\n\n5. Invoice Product Association Management\nRecord the products and quantities contained in each invoice.\nAssociating invoice and product information with invoice ID and product ID.\nYou can query the products and quantities contained in each invoice, as well as the detailed information of the products.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0352.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0352\nCREATE TABLE `supplier` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `purchase_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `selling_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `min_stock_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `supplier` (`supplier_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `tax_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `total_value` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice_product` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`invoice_id`) REFERENCES `invoice` (`invoice_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
